<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Duke of Saxony</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> was the ruler of the duchy of Saxony in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-bull-of-1356">Golden Bull of 1356</a> the Duke of Saxony was one of the seven prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a> entitled to elect the emperor, alongside the archbishops of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trier">Trier</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-of-bohemia">King of Bohemia</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/count-palatine">Count Palatine</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/margrave-of-brandenburg">Margrave of Brandenburg</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/duke-of-saxony.jpg" alt="Duke of Saxony" width="320" height="403" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Glasshouse, using elements by Sodacan, Trondivers and katepanomegas · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_Arms_of_the_Kingdom_of_Saxony_1806-1918.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
